IMPORT prelude

-- Presbyterian Church of England Mission Ordinance 1903 (Singapore) -- who is the Corporation "The Senior Missionary in Singapore of
-- the Foreign Missions of the Presbyterian Church of England" (s 2(1)) and when a successor is duly qualified (s 4), what the Ordinance
-- empowers it to do (s 2(2), (3)), how its deeds are validly sealed and signed (s 3), which lands of the preamble it vests and for what
-- estate (s 5), and whose rights the Ordinance leaves alone (s 6).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PCEMO1903.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The only amendment
-- annotation in the body is "[7/97]" under s 6; the legislative history lists Act 7 of 1997 (Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act
-- 1997, in force 1 October 1997) as its last entry. The Ordinance is dated 8 May 1903.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0242 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- The Ordinance has six sections, so the whole of it is in scope. For a person outside the Mission it matters in two places: dealing
-- with the Corporation over land (s 2(3), s 3, s 4), and title to the seven parcels the preamble recites (s 5, s 6).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); the content of s 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, to which s 3(1) refers (whether a
-- power of attorney has been "deposited" under it is taken as a stated fact); the conditions of the recited leases and grants beyond
-- the term, rent and purpose the preamble states; the internal governance of the Foreign Missions Committee, about which the Ordinance
-- says nothing.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Presbyterian Church of England Mission Ordinance 1903 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2(1) and 4 -- who is the Corporation, and when a successor is duly qualified`

-- s 2(1): "The Reverend John Angus Bethune Cook and his successors for the time being in the office of Senior Missionary of the said
-- Committee duly qualified as hereinafter provided shall be a body corporate (hereinafter called the Corporation)", with perpetual
-- succession and a corporate seal.
-- s 4(1): no successor "shall be deemed to be duly qualified as aforesaid unless and until he has caused an extract from the minutes of
-- the Foreign Missions Committee of the Presbyterian Church of England appointing him such Senior Missionary, certified as correct by
-- the Convenor of the Foreign Missions Committee ..., to have been filed in the office of the Minister, and unless and until a
-- notification of such filing has appeared in the Gazette."
-- s 4(2): "Such notification shall be sufficient evidence of the appointment and that the person named therein is duly qualified".
--
-- Four steps, all required: appointment by the Committee, the Convenor's certificate, filing with the Minister, and the Gazette
-- notification. Mr Cook, named in s 2(1), needed none of them. The notification is "sufficient" evidence, not "conclusive".
DECLARE Claimant HAS
    `is the Reverend John Angus Bethune Cook` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is appointed Senior Missionary by the Foreign Missions Committee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the minute extract is certified by the Convenor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the extract is filed in the office of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the filing is notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a duly qualified successor` IF
        `the claimant`'s `is appointed Senior Missionary by the Foreign Missions Committee`
    AND `the claimant`'s `the minute extract is certified by the Convenor`
    AND `the claimant`'s `the extract is filed in the office of the Minister`
    AND `the claimant`'s `the filing is notified in the Gazette`

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds the office that is the Corporation` IF
        `the claimant`'s `is the Reverend John Angus Bethune Cook`
    OR  `is a duly qualified successor` `the claimant`

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Gazette notification is sufficient evidence of qualification` IF
    `the claimant`'s `the filing is notified in the Gazette`

§§ `2(2) and 2(3) -- what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do`

-- s 2(2): "The said seal may from time to time be broken, changed, altered, or made anew as the Corporation thinks fit."
-- s 2(3): "The Corporation may acquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property of every description, and may
-- sell, convey, assign, surrender and yield up, mortgage, demise, reassign, transfer or otherwise dispose of any movable and immovable
-- property vested in the Corporation upon such terms as the Corporation thinks fit."
--
-- The powers of disposal reach only property "vested in the Corporation". Unlike the Bishop of Singapore Ordinance 1911, this Ordinance
-- contains no words about suing or being sued; whether the general law supplies that capacity is outside the text and not encoded.
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `use and change its corporate seal`
    `acquire or purchase property`
    `hold and enjoy property`
    `sell property`
    `mortgage property`
    `lease property`
    `transfer or otherwise dispose of property`
    `sue or be sued`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `the property is vested in the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `use and change its corporate seal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `acquire or purchase property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `hold and enjoy property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sell property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `mortgage property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `lease property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `transfer or otherwise dispose of property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3 -- sealing and signing the Corporation's instruments`

-- s 3(1): instruments requiring the seal "shall be sealed with the seal of the Corporation in the presence of the Reverend John Angus
-- Bethune Cook, or his attorney duly authorised by a power of attorney deposited under section 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of
-- Property Act 1886, or in the presence of his successor for the time being in the office of Senior Missionary, or his attorney duly
-- authorised as aforesaid, and shall also be signed by the said John Angus Bethune Cook or his attorney, or by his successor or his
-- attorney."
-- s 3(2): "Such signing shall be sufficient evidence of the due sealing of such deeds, documents and other instruments."
--
-- READING: s 3(1) says "his successor for the time being in the office of Senior Missionary" without repeating "duly qualified". Because
-- s 2(1) makes only duly qualified successors the Corporation, a successor not yet gazetted is treated here as unable to execute. This
-- is a reading of ss 2(1) and 4 together, not words of s 3.
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `the Reverend John Angus Bethune Cook`
    `a duly qualified successor`
    `an attorney under a deposited power of attorney`
    `an attorney whose power of attorney is not deposited`
    `a successor appointed but not yet gazetted`
    `a church elder with no power of attorney`
    `nobody`

DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `is sealed with the Corporation seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sealed in the presence of` IS AN Officer
    `signed by` IS AN Officer

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may witness the seal and sign` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `the Reverend John Angus Bethune Cook` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a duly qualified successor` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an attorney under a deposited power of attorney` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is executed as section 3 requires` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `may witness the seal and sign` (`the instrument`'s `sealed in the presence of`)
    AND `may witness the seal and sign` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence of due sealing` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `may witness the seal and sign` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

§§ `5 and preamble -- the lands vested in the Corporation`

-- Preamble: (a) leases No. 241 (dated 1 August 1840) and No. 242 (dated 1 July 1840), Prinsep Street, from the East India Company,
-- "for the terms of 99 years at the yearly rents of $3"; (b) lease No. 1646, Upper Tanglin, General No. 4920, "for the term of 999
-- years from 8 November 1880 at the rent of $1", on condition "that it should be used for the purpose of the Chinese Mission and that
-- should it be used for any other purpose it would revert to Government"; (c) lease No. 1918 dated 28 January 1885, Amokiah, General
-- No. 5506, "for the term of 999 years from the date of the lease at the rent of $1"; (d) Statutory Land Grant No. 2675, Amokio, Survey
-- No. 6244, "for ever for the purposes of the English Presbyterian Mission, and for no other purposes whatsoever"; (e) Statutory Land
-- Grant No. 3772, Bukit Timah, Survey No. 11774, "for ever for religious purposes of the Chinese Mission ... and for no other purposes
-- whatsoever at the annual rent of $1"; (f) "20 several allotments being Lots 114 to 128, both inclusive, and 149 to 153, both
-- inclusive", Kallang District, assured by Foo Teng Quee and Ong Sam Leong "in fee simple upon trust".
-- s 5: "Each of the pieces of land mentioned in the preamble is hereby vested in the Corporation for an estate in fee simple, or for the
-- residue of the term of years under which the same is held, as the case may be, free from all trusts whatever."
--
-- The two Statutory Land Grants "for ever" are treated as fee simple; that is an inference from "for ever" and "as the case may be".
-- The years a term ends are simple arithmetic from the preamble (start year plus term); the Ordinance itself states no end date.
-- The Prinsep Street terms began in 1840 and ran 99 years, so on that arithmetic they ended in 1939.
DECLARE Parcel IS ONE OF
    `Prinsep Street lease No. 241`
    `Prinsep Street lease No. 242`
    `Upper Tanglin lease No. 1646`
    `Amokiah lease No. 1918`
    `Amokio Statutory Land Grant No. 2675`
    `Bukit Timah Statutory Land Grant No. 3772`
    `the Kallang allotments`
    `land not mentioned in the preamble`

DECLARE Estate IS ONE OF
    `fee simple`
    `residue of the term of years`
    `nothing`

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is held under a term of years` IF
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `Prinsep Street lease No. 241` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Prinsep Street lease No. 242` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Upper Tanglin lease No. 1646` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Amokiah lease No. 1918` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5 vests it in the Corporation` IF
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `land not mentioned in the preamble` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH AN Estate
DECIDE `the estate vested by section 5` IS
    IF NOT `section 5 vests it in the Corporation` `the parcel`
    THEN `nothing`
    ELSE IF `is held under a term of years` `the parcel`
         THEN `residue of the term of years`
         ELSE `fee simple`

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `term in years` IS
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `Prinsep Street lease No. 241` THEN 99
    WHEN `Prinsep Street lease No. 242` THEN 99
    WHEN `Upper Tanglin lease No. 1646` THEN 999
    WHEN `Amokiah lease No. 1918` THEN 999
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `year the term began` IS
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `Prinsep Street lease No. 241` THEN 1840
    WHEN `Prinsep Street lease No. 242` THEN 1840
    WHEN `Upper Tanglin lease No. 1646` THEN 1880
    WHEN `Amokiah lease No. 1918` THEN 1885
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `year the term ends` IS
    `year the term began` `the parcel` + `term in years` `the parcel`

-- "A residue remains" in a year is read as: the parcel is held for a term, and the term's end year is later than that year. This is the
-- encoding's year-granular approximation; the leases run from particular days.
GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel, `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a residue of the term remains in` IF
        `is held under a term of years` `the parcel`
    AND `year the term ends` `the parcel` > `the year`

-- The rents stated in the preamble, in dollars a year; 0 where the preamble states no rent.
GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `rent stated in the preamble` IS
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `Prinsep Street lease No. 241` THEN 3
    WHEN `Prinsep Street lease No. 242` THEN 3
    WHEN `Upper Tanglin lease No. 1646` THEN 1
    WHEN `Amokiah lease No. 1918` THEN 1
    WHEN `Bukit Timah Statutory Land Grant No. 3772` THEN 1
    OTHERWISE 0

-- The preamble records a restriction on use for three parcels: lease No. 1646 (Chinese Mission, reverting to Government on other use),
-- Grant No. 2675 and Grant No. 3772 ("for no other purposes whatsoever").
GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the preamble records a purpose restriction` IF
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `Upper Tanglin lease No. 1646` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Amokio Statutory Land Grant No. 2675` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Bukit Timah Statutory Land Grant No. 3772` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the preamble records a reverter to Government` IF
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `Upper Tanglin lease No. 1646` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The Kallang allotments: "Lots 114 to 128, both inclusive, and 149 to 153, both inclusive" -- the preamble calls them "20 several
-- allotments". The count is checked from the ranges.
GIVEN `first lot` IS A NUMBER, `last lot` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `lots in an inclusive range` IS
    `last lot` - `first lot` + 1

DECIDE `number of Kallang allotments` IS
    `lots in an inclusive range` 114 128 + `lots in an inclusive range` 149 153

§§ `6 -- whose rights are saved`

-- s 6: "Nothing in this Ordinance shall affect the rights of the Government, or of any bodies politic or corporate, or of any other
-- persons except those mentioned in this Ordinance, and those claiming by, from or under them."
--
-- READING: the Government is named first and separately, so its rights are treated as saved whether or not the Crown or the Governor is
-- "mentioned" in the preamble (they are, as lessor and grantor). The persons mentioned include the London Missionary Society, the
-- Foreign Missions Committee, and the Kallang vendors Foo Teng Quee and Ong Sam Leong; their rights, and those of persons claiming
-- through them, are not saved by s 6. This is a reading of the punctuation, not a stated rule.
DECLARE Party IS ONE OF
    `the Government`
    `the London Missionary Society`
    `the Foreign Missions Committee`
    `Foo Teng Quee or Ong Sam Leong`
    `a person claiming under the London Missionary Society`
    `a neighbour not mentioned in the Ordinance`
    `a company not mentioned in the Ordinance`

GIVEN `the party` IS A Party
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance may affect their rights` IF
    CONSIDER `the party`
    WHEN `the Government` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a neighbour not mentioned in the Ordinance` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a company not mentioned in the Ordinance` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- READING: s 5 vests the land "free from all trusts whatever", but s 6 saves the Government's rights. The Government's reverter on
-- lease No. 1646 is therefore treated as surviving the vesting. This is an inference from ss 5 and 6 together.
GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government's reverter survives the vesting` IF
        `section 5 vests it in the Corporation` `the parcel`
    AND `the preamble records a reverter to Government` `the parcel`
    AND NOT `the Ordinance may affect their rights` `the Government`
